# 2. Redis Key Design (Very Important)

Designing good keys is critical in distributed systems.

We store history like this:

```
track:{camera_id}:{track_id}
```

Example:

```
track:cam_1:606
```

Value stored:

```
list of recent frames
```

Example:

```json
[
  {"frame":600,"bbox":[...],"timestamp":...},
  {"frame":605,"bbox":[...],"timestamp":...},
  {"frame":610,"bbox":[...],"timestamp":...}
]
```

Redis command used:

```
LPUSH
LTRIM
EXPIRE
```

This keeps **only recent history**.

